From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:34:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: async pathfinding

Behind async.async-pathfinding.enabled (default false). With the key off the
node evaluator generator is null and PathFinder#findPath runs the vanilla
search on the calling thread.

With the key on, the request is prepared on the entity's thread (evaluator of
its own, start node, targets), only the A* runs on a pool with a heap and a
neighbour array per thread, and the result is copied into the path by the
entity's thread the first time it asks (Path#isProcessed) or cannot wait
(AsyncPath#process, which then searches on the spot). A request replaced in
the meantime is never applied to the navigation.

Derived from Petal "Async Pathfinding" (peaches94, GPL-3.0-only),
https://github.com/Bloom-host/Petal, fixed and updated by Kaiiju
(GPL-3.0-only), https://github.com/KaiijuMC/Kaiiju, as carried by Leaf
(patch "Petal: Async Pathfinding"; HaHaWTH, Taiyou06, Altiami, MrlingXD,
hayanesuru), GPL-3.0, https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf. Compared with
DivineMC's port (NONPLAYT, BX Team), which prepares on the pool.

Not ported, on purpose: amphibious navigation, the sniffer and the creaking
keep the synchronous search (their evaluator or mob rewrites a malus around
it); Leaf's POI, sensor, Mob and ShulkerBoxBlock hunks; its queue policies
that drop or flush searches.

